     "text": "I fixed `top_words` in `textstats.py` so that words with equal counts come out in alphabetical order. The tests pass, including the existing ones.\n\nThe old code sorted only by count, with `reverse=True`. The sort key is now `(-count, word)`, so higher counts come first and ties break alphabetically.\n\nI added `test_top_ties_alphabetical` to `test_textstats.py`. It uses your example: `top_words(\"pear apple pear apple fig\", 3)` returns `[(\"apple\", 2), (\"pear\", 2), (\"fig\", 1)]`.",
